# Plato NUG subset — 3 instances, pinned. Part of the fourth set's
# diversity half.
#
# Everything about why this set exists, where it comes from, the licence
# position, the no-reference tier and the row/col counting rule is in
# `bench/plato-pds.manifest`. Read that first; nothing is restated here.
#
#     make plato-nug
#
# Served from https://plato.asu.edu/ftp/lptestset/nug/, `bz2-emps`.
#
# LP lower bounds for quadratic assignment problems: S. E. Karisch and
# F. Rendl, "Lower bounds for the quadratic assignment problem via triangle
# decompositions", Mathematical Programming 71(2), 1995, 137-152; and
# K. G. Ramakrishnan, M. G. C. Resende, B. Ramachandran and J. F. Pekny,
# "Tight QAP bounds via linear programming", in Combinatorial and Global
# Optimization, World Scientific, 2002, 297-303.
#
# These are the shape the tree does not have. Every model JAOS reads today is
# an economic, transport or stochastic LP; a QAP relaxation is dense-blocked
# and structurally unlike all of them. nug30 is 52260 x 379350 and expands to
# 58.6 MB, the largest MPS in any of the four sets.
#
# The row-count cross-check against Mittelmann's published table shows **no**
# offset for nug08-3rd, where pds and fome are one apart. That is recorded and
# not explained; see the pds manifest.
#
#     name  sha256  rows  cols  reference  source  objconst
#
nug08-3rd    1dadc68c4b9f57f95e0bb450fb2d495c0cd9a53a591764b99b03c0a6d37e7df0 19728 20448 0.0 none 0.0
nug20        124a1ea609b8b4ef692733470eac386454a332e211115680e21b873c6235e4da 15240 72600 0.0 none 0.0
nug30        1bed0e56844920c278f266e825abf03cd08d01cccd01dc768e731ffbf9501030 52260 379350 0.0 none 0.0
